// Round 423 -- shared base64 data URI for the VIEENT badge mark, used by
// the next/og opengraph-image routes (app/pick-package/[token]/opengraph-image.js
// and friends). next/og's edge runtime cannot reach the filesystem or
// /public at request time the way a normal React component can (no fs,
// and fetching our own /public asset over the network at request time is
// fragile pre-deploy / on preview URLs), so the asset is embedded as a
// data: URI here instead and consumed via a plain <img src=... /> inside
// the ImageResponse tree, which next/og supports natively.
//
// Source file: public/brand/vieent-badge.png (the same white/transparent
// mark BottomBar.js uses for dark theme -- see lib/BottomBar.js). If the
// badge art ever changes, regenerate this constant from the new PNG:
//   python3 -c "import base64; print(base64.b64encode(open('public/brand/vieent-badge.png','rb').read()).decode())"
// and paste the output back in below.
export const VIEENT_BADGE_DATA_URI =
  "data:image/png;base64,";

// Round 424 -- same reasoning as VIEENT_BADGE_DATA_URI above: next/og's
// edge runtime can't read /public at request time, so this is embedded
// as a data URI too. Source file: public/brand/vsounder-cover-spotify.jpg
// (the "A HOME FOR INDEPENDENT ARTISTS" orange cover banner, originally
// downloaded as "Spotify-Cover-Profile-VIEENT.png" but the bytes are
// actually JPEG -- `file` on the original confirmed "JPEG image data" --
// renamed to .jpg and this data URI's mime type set to image/jpeg to
// match; the first attempt at this shipped mislabeled as image/png,
// which next/og's renderer (satori) silently failed to decode, and the
// background just never appeared) -- used as the background of the
// VSounder channel-reference magic link's share-preview card
// (app/channels/[token]/opengraph-image.js) and, at low opacity, as a
// background watermark on the live page itself
// (app/channels/[token]/page.js) -- that second use reads straight from
// /public since page.js is a normal client component with no edge-runtime
// restriction, so it does NOT need this constant.
export const VSOUNDER_COVER_DATA_URI =
  "data:image/jpeg;base64,";

// Round 425 -- same reasoning as the other *_DATA_URI constants above:
// next/og's edge runtime can't read /public at request time. Both used
// by the redesigned app/channels/[token]/opengraph-image.js (light-theme
// share-preview card, per explicit "im not happy with the og vsounder
// preview5 png ... let me clarify" follow-up correction).
//
// Source: public/brand/vieent-badge-orange.png -- cropped from the raw
// master the user dropped in a newly-connected "vieent badge" folder
// (VIEENT-BADGE-nonshape 2.png) down to just the orange circular mark.
// That master file also contains a white "VIEENT" wordmark to the left
// of the circle (meant for BottomBar.js's dark-theme rendering, see that
// file's own comment) -- solid white pixels, not transparent, so on this
// light-theme card they'd have gone invisible instead of just not being
// wanted. Cropped in code (not by hand) to the circle's actual colored
// pixels (a numpy alpha+color-diff mask, not a fixed guess at
// coordinates) rather than reused whole.
export const VIEENT_BADGE_ORANGE_DATA_URI =
  "data:image/png;base64,";

// Source: public/brand/vsounder-wordmark-light.png (the existing asset
// page.js already uses for light theme -- the cursive black "VSounder"
// logo + "empowered by VIEENT" tagline, correctly dark-colored for a
// light background, as opposed to -dark.png which is for dark
// backgrounds despite the confusingly inverted-sounding name -- see
// page.js's `/brand/vsounder-wordmark-${themeLock || "dark"}.png`).
// Used in place of the plain "Channel Reference" text heading.
export const VSOUNDER_WORDMARK_LIGHT_DATA_URI =
  "data:image/png;base64,";
